<servinfo servinfosgmlid = "AENKSB0A9B06013" svcinfotypenbr = "08" svcinfoqualnbr = "01" supplyoff = "1" modify = "0">
<title>
B-Pillar Outer Panel, Rear Door Hinge Reinforcement and Center Pillar Inner Panel Removal and Installation
</title>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGSB0A9B0089.jpg" width = "183.000mm" height = "104.891mm" ver = "01" gw = "341" gh = "281"/>
</figure>
<servinfosub id = "AENKSB0A9B06013001">
<title>
General Notes
</title>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Welding method and number of welding points are the same on both sides. This repair instruction shows procedure for left side.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Part filled with foamed material is included in parts of this repair. Therefore, repair referring to 
<intxref refid = "AENKSB0A9B06024">Foamed Material Filling Area Repair</intxref>
 for precautions and repair procedure.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
The dimensions shown in the figure are reference values when cutting replacement part placed on top of existing part. Determine the most appropriate cutting (or joint) line considering both size of replacement part and condition of existing part.
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</servinfosub>
<servinfosub id = "AENKSB0A9B06013002">
<title>
Removal
</title>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Mark at the shown position and cut B-pillar outer panel, rear door hinge reinforcement and center pillar inner panel at the same time at shown rough cutting position.
</ptxt>
<attention4>
<ptxt>
You may accidentally cut the parts under the B-pillar outer panel when cutting the B-pillar outer panel.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Take sufficient care not to damage the parts under the B-pillar outer panel when cutting the B-pillar outer panel.
</ptxt>
</attention4>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Cut B-pillar outer panel, rear door hinge reinforcement and center pillar inner panel at the same time at shown rough cutting position.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Drill out welding spots.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Bend open 2 metal tabs (arrow) and remove B-pillar outer panel.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGSB0A9B0090.jpg" width = "183.000mm" height = "177.496mm" ver = "03" gw = "455" gh = "487"/>
<callout>
<table frame = "all" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<tgroup cols = "2" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<colspec colnum = "1" colname = "1" colwidth = "0.394in"/>
<colspec colnum = "2" colname = "2" colwidth = "6.693in"/>
<tbody>
<row rowsep = "1">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
<symbol name = "MANOTE" width = "5.132mm" height = "3.048mm"/>
:
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
When heating around foamed material application portion to detach foamed material, be sure that temperature of said portion does not reach 170 &#176;C (338 &#176;F).
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row rowsep = "0">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
1.
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
B-pillar outer panel cut position (Cut around here)
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</callout>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Drill out welding spots and remove upper part of rear door hinge reinforcement and upper part of center pillar inner panel.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGSB0A9B0091.jpg" width = "183.000mm" height = "52.390mm" ver = "02" gw = "468" gh = "132"/>
<callout>
<table frame = "all" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
